// Undermere's items: what lies under the lake and what the dead leave behind.
// Where each thing is found lying about, and how often, is `item_spawns.ron`.
//
// Every field (the ones marked "optional" may be left out):
//   name:       unique; the spawn table and drops refer to it; one of it, singular, since
//               the engine says a stack as "12 arrows", so a thing counted by its measure is
//               named by it: "gold coin", never "gold"
//   glyph:      one character, and one the typeface in `assets/fonts/` has
//   color:      (r, g, b) in 0..=1; a thing wearing a face from `lore.ron` is drawn in the
//               face's colour instead, known or not, so its colour gives nothing away
//   price:      optional; the price of one at level nought, from the spec's tables; absent
//               on gold, which is not for sale. `armory.rs`'s `keep_worth` turns it into the
//               engine's `Worth`, current on the thing rather than saved: 100 added a level
//               the adventurer knows above nought, an unfamiliar level counted as nought, and
//               no `Worth` at all for a kind not known, a curse's sign shown, or a level known
//               below nought
//   slot:       optional; where it is worn: "main hand" | "off hand" | "head" | "body" |
//               "left finger" | "right finger" | "light"
//   either:     optional; true for a thing that fits either slot of the pair its slot is one
//               of: a one-handed weapon either hand, "main hand" | "off hand", and a ring
//               either hand's finger, "left finger" | "right finger"
//   also:       optional; slots it also claims when worn, for a two-hander
//   tags:       optional; "weapon" | "armor" | "potion" | "scroll" | "staff" | "wand" | "ring" |
//               "gold" | "arrow" | "light" | "thrown" | "artifact"; what a chest's row asks for
//               by tag, what a keeper buys, the curio every tag a priced thing carries, so an
//               artifact carries its own for the curio to buy it by, and the kinds a floor's
//               things are drawn by: potions, scrolls, weapons, armor,
//               staffs, wands, rings and thrown things, each kind as often as `finds.rs` weighs
//               it and each thing of a kind as `item_spawns.ron` does. A weapon, armor,
//               ring, staff or wand that does not stack takes levels: each level adds one to a
//               weapon's every damage roll and five to its wielder's accuracy, one to armor's
//               armor, and what per_level says; one below nought is cursed, and will not come off
//               once it is put on. A potion, scroll, staff, wand or ring wears a face from
//               `lore.ron` until its kind is known
//   effects:    optional; [(kind:, chance:, args:)] what the thing holds, written as an
//               ability's effects are in abilities.ron: the engine's Harm(kind:, roll:),
//               Mend(roll:), Inflict(status:, turns:), Cleanse(status:), Ignite(turns:) and
//               Emit(gas:, amount:), a cloud of "paralytic" | "confusing" | "darkness" a full
//               cell being 255, the statuses being "poisoned" | "scorched" | "mending" |
//               "regenerating" | "chilled" | "slowed" | "hasted" | "fireproof" | "shrouded" |
//               "paralysed" | "confused"; and Undermere's own besides: Enchant,
//               one more level on the thing a use is made on; Identify, that thing made known;
//               RemoveCurse, everything the user wears free to come off; Strengthen(by:), the
//               user's strength raised by that much for good; Life(by:), the user's greatest
//               health raised by that much for good and their health made whole; Descend, the
//               user sunk to a free cell of the floor below, and nothing on the deepest;
//               Darkness(turns:, amount:), everyone where it lands shrouded that many turns and
//               that much darkness given off on every cell of it; Blink(reach:, per_level:), the
//               user along the line aimed, up to reach cells and per_level more for each of
//               the thing's effect_per_level amount; TeleportOther, whoever it strikes sent far
//               off; Beckon, whoever it strikes pulled to the user's side; Polymorph, whoever
//               it strikes made a monster of another kind at the same share of its health;
//               Plenty, whoever it strikes made two at half its health each; Conjure(blades:,
//               turns:), that many spectral blades on the user's side for that many turns, one
//               more and each blow one harder for each of the thing's amount; Dominate, whoever
//               it strikes bound to the user's side, surely at a quarter of its health or under
//               and otherwise as often in a hundred as it has lost; Teleport, the user sent to a
//               free cell far off, in place of the engine's own; Recharge, every staff the user
//               carries full and every wand a charge more; MagicMapping, the floor's layout
//               known; Discord(turns:), every foe in sight at odds with everyone for that many
//               turns; Aggravate, a shriek and every monster on the floor aware of the user;
//               Summon(fewest:, most:), that many of the floor's monsters beside the user, aware
//               of them. Each of Undermere's own takes
//               only the arguments it names, and none where it names none. Landed by any trigger
//               with no list of its own
//   triggers:   optional; [(on:, area:, fires:, effects:, look:, every:, targeting:, asks:)] what it
//               does at its moments: on is "use" (used from the pack; lands on the user, or where
//               it is aimed) | "land" (a throw comes to rest) | "fire" (an attack is made with it) |
//               "hit" (that attack strikes) | "pulse" (a worn thing's clock came round); area is
//               Here (default) | Burst(radius:); fires is how many times it may go off, every
//               time when left out; effects is its own list, the thing's shared effects when
//               left out; look is optional, (glyph:, color: (r:, g:, b:)) in bytes, shown over
//               every cell it lands on and flying there for an aimed use, which must have one,
//               or its zap is never seen; every is hundredths of a step between pulses, required
//               on a "pulse" trigger, refused on any other, and a "pulse" trigger is for a worn
//               thing; targeting is optional, (mode:, aim:, sight:), and only on a thing's one
//               "use" trigger, for a staff or a wand used at somewhere and
//               pointed as an ability in abilities.ron is: mode Own | Adjacent | Bolt(range:) |
//               Ball(range:, radius:) | Beam(range:) | Cone(length:), aim what it wants under it,
//               Foe (default) | Ally | Ground | Anyone, and sight whether the cell it is pointed
//               at must be seen, true when left out; the pack's use key then opens the cursor;
//               asks is optional, (prompt:, tag:), and only on a thing's one "use" trigger with
//               no targeting, for a scroll read onto another of the user's things: prompt is what the
//               choice is asked under, tag one of the tags above that the thing chosen must
//               carry, any thing carried but itself when left out; the pack's use key then
//               chooses, and the use lands on the user with the thing chosen for the game's own
//               effects. Asking tells that a thing is one of the kinds that ask, so a thing
//               not yet known is named the moment the pack asks for it, and backing out of the
//               choice spends nothing
//   consumable: optional; (charges:, when_empty:, per_level:, recharge:) what a use or a
//               landing costs it: charges a fresh one holds at level nought, Destroyed | Kept at
//               the last, per_level, optional, the charges each level adds, for a thing that
//               takes levels, and recharge, optional, the whole turns a spent charge takes to
//               come back at level one, divided by the level above it; absent, a spent charge
//               is gone until something refills it
//   effect_per_level: optional; (amount:, turns:) what each level adds to whatever its
//               triggers land, either left out for nothing: amount to every Harm and Mend roll
//               and to Undermere's own effects' reach and number, turns to every status; only
//               on a thing that takes levels
//   found_at:   optional; (lowest, highest) the levels it is found at, drawn evenly: a wand's
//               charges; absent, a ring is found at one to three or cursed below nought, a
//               staff at two and better deeper, a weapon or armor plain, better deeper or
//               cursed, and anything else at nought; only on a thing that takes levels
//   armor:      optional; flat armor while worn
//   resists:    optional; [(damage kind, percent removed)] while worn: "slash" | "pierce" |
//               "crush" | "fire" | "cold" | "poison"
//   melee:      optional; (roll:, kind:, look:, shape:, unaware:) while wielded, roll as
//               "NdS+B"; look is optional, (glyph:, color: (r:, g:, b:)) in bytes, and a blow
//               bursts in its colour on everyone it strikes; shape is optional, Sweep, every
//               foe beside the wielder struck too, or Pierce(n), the foes in the next n cells
//               behind the target, the target alone when left out; unaware is optional, what
//               a blow on a foe that has not noticed the wielder is worth in percent, in
//               place of the house's three hundred
//   ranged:     optional; (range:, effective:, roll:, kind:, look:) while wielded; effective
//               is optional, the furthest cell with no range penalty, a third of range when
//               absent; look is optional, what a shot flies as
//   ammo:       optional; a tag from the list above, what one shot spends from the wielder's
//               pack; with none of it there the weapon is dry and does not shoot; only on a
//               thing with a ranged attack
//   throw:      optional; (range:, effective:, strike:) when thrown, effective as for ranged,
//               strike optional as (roll, kind) for the blow it deals whoever it hits;
//               absent, it cannot be thrown
//   cost:       optional; what one blow or shot with it costs, in hundredths of a step;
//               absent is 100
//   light:      optional; the light it sheds where it lies and from whoever carries it, as
//               (radius: tiles, color: (r, g, b) in 0..=1, flicker: 0..=1, may be left out)
//   lends:      optional; names from `traits.ron` it gives whoever wears it, while it is worn;
//               only on a thing with a slot, and two lent traits may not set one value
//   strength:   optional; the strength it asks of whoever wears it: each point they are short
//               costs a weapon's wielder four accuracy and armor's wearer one armor; only on a
//               thing with a slot
//   bestows:    optional; [(stat, amount)] added to its wearer's stats while it is worn, whatever
//               its level: "strength" | "accuracy" | "evasion" | "speed" | "stealth" |
//               "mending" | "light" | "armor" | "footfall" | "regeneration" | "wisdom" |
//               "reaping" | "awareness" | "quiet"; footfall is how many steps of loudness each
//               of the wearer's steps carries, two for anyone, and heavy armor adds to it;
//               regeneration is health back a hundred turns, wisdom percent faster every
//               carried staff refills, reaping turns off each carried staff's next charge for
//               every blow that lands, one a swing however many it strikes, awareness points
//               added to the chance a turn of spotting what is hidden, and quiet taken off
//               every watcher's certain notice of the wearer, so a value below nought, the
//               Crown of Grubnak's own gleam, widens it; only on a thing with a slot
//   per_level:  optional; [(stat, amount)] added to its wearer's stats for each of its levels
//               while it is worn, and taken away for each below nought; only on a thing with a
//               slot that takes levels
//   stack:      optional; whether copies merge into one counted entry; never on a worn thing
//   pile:       optional; how many make a pile where one is found, as "NdS+B", times the
//               floor it is found on; only on a thing that stacks; absent, one
#![enable(implicit_some)]
[
    // The weapons, each with the trade it makes. A dagger is a light blade
    // that strikes a foe that has not noticed its wielder five times over,
    // where any other blow strikes three; an axe sweeps every foe round
    // its wielder, and a spear runs on through to the foe behind; a mace
    // and a war hammer take two turns a blow and hit the harder for it;
    // the two-handers leave no hand for a shield; and the heavier the
    // weapon, the more strength it asks. A blow that strikes more than
    // its target bursts on each foe it strikes, so a sweep is seen to go
    // round; the bow's arrow is seen to fly.
    (name: "dagger", glyph: ')', color: (0.75, 0.75, 0.8), price: 30, slot: "main hand", either: true, tags: ["weapon"], melee: (roll: "1d4+1", kind: "pierce", unaware: 500), strength: 10),
    (name: "sword", glyph: ')', color: (0.8, 0.82, 0.9), price: 60, slot: "main hand", either: true, tags: ["weapon"], melee: (roll: "1d7+1", kind: "slash"), strength: 12),
    (name: "broadsword", glyph: ')', color: (0.88, 0.9, 0.98), price: 120, slot: "main hand", also: ["off hand"], tags: ["weapon"], melee: (roll: "2d6+1", kind: "slash"), strength: 14),
    (name: "axe", glyph: ')', color: (0.7, 0.62, 0.5), price: 80, slot: "main hand", tags: ["weapon"], strength: 13,
     melee: (roll: "1d7", kind: "slash", shape: Sweep, look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 235, g: 225, b: 205)))),
    (name: "war axe", glyph: ')', color: (0.62, 0.52, 0.4), price: 150, slot: "main hand", also: ["off hand"], tags: ["weapon"], strength: 15,
     melee: (roll: "2d5", kind: "slash", shape: Sweep, look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 235, g: 225, b: 205)))),
    (name: "mace", glyph: ')', color: (0.62, 0.62, 0.66), price: 70, slot: "main hand", tags: ["weapon"], melee: (roll: "2d6+2", kind: "crush"), cost: 200, strength: 16),
    (name: "war hammer", glyph: ')', color: (0.55, 0.55, 0.62), price: 140, slot: "main hand", also: ["off hand"], tags: ["weapon"], melee: (roll: "3d6+2", kind: "crush"), cost: 200, strength: 20),
    (name: "spear", glyph: ')', color: (0.72, 0.62, 0.45), price: 60, slot: "main hand", tags: ["weapon"], strength: 13,
     melee: (roll: "1d8+1", kind: "pierce", shape: Pierce(1), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 205, g: 220, b: 240)))),
    (name: "war pike", glyph: ')', color: (0.64, 0.56, 0.42), price: 130, slot: "main hand", also: ["off hand"], tags: ["weapon"], strength: 18,
     melee: (roll: "2d6+2", kind: "pierce", shape: Pierce(1), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 205, g: 220, b: 240)))),
    // ANCHOR: bow
    (name: "bow", glyph: '}', color: (0.65, 0.5, 0.32), price: 80, slot: "main hand", also: ["off hand"], tags: ["weapon"], ammo: "arrow", strength: 12,
     ranged: (range: 8, effective: 5, roll: "1d6+1", kind: "pierce", look: (glyph: '|', color: (r: 191, g: 173, b: 128)))),
    // What is thrown, found by the handful: arrows, which the bow spends
    // a shot at a time and which fly badly from the hand, and darts and
    // javelins, made to be thrown and picked up again where they land.
    (name: "arrow", glyph: '|', color: (0.75, 0.68, 0.5), price: 2, tags: ["arrow", "thrown"], stack: true, throw: (range: 4, strike: ("1d2", "pierce"))),
    // ANCHOR_END: bow
    (name: "dart", glyph: '|', color: (0.7, 0.72, 0.78), price: 3, tags: ["thrown"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6, effective: 4, strike: ("1d3", "pierce"))),
    (name: "javelin", glyph: '/', color: (0.7, 0.6, 0.42), price: 8, tags: ["thrown"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6, effective: 4, strike: ("2d4", "pierce"))),
    // The armor: the heavier, the more it turns, the more strength it
    // asks, and the louder every step taken in it, which whatever has ears
    // hears the further off. A shield turns one blow in ten aside, the
    // one thing under the lake that does.
    (name: "leather armor", glyph: '[', color: (0.6, 0.45, 0.3), price: 40, slot: "body", tags: ["armor"], armor: 1, strength: 10),
    (name: "scale mail", glyph: '[', color: (0.55, 0.62, 0.55), price: 100, slot: "body", tags: ["armor"], armor: 2, strength: 13, bestows: [("footfall", 1)]),
    (name: "chain mail", glyph: '[', color: (0.68, 0.7, 0.75), price: 160, slot: "body", tags: ["armor"], armor: 3, strength: 13, bestows: [("footfall", 1)]),
    (name: "banded mail", glyph: '[', color: (0.72, 0.62, 0.48), price: 240, slot: "body", tags: ["armor"], armor: 4, strength: 15, bestows: [("footfall", 2)]),
    (name: "splint mail", glyph: '[', color: (0.6, 0.65, 0.75), price: 320, slot: "body", tags: ["armor"], armor: 5, strength: 17, bestows: [("footfall", 2)]),
    (name: "plate armor", glyph: '[', color: (0.82, 0.84, 0.9), price: 450, slot: "body", tags: ["armor"], armor: 6, strength: 19, bestows: [("footfall", 3)]),
    (name: "shield", glyph: ']', color: (0.62, 0.52, 0.4), price: 60, slot: "off hand", tags: ["armor"], armor: 1, strength: 12, bestows: [("evasion", 10)]),
    (name: "helm", glyph: '^', color: (0.7, 0.7, 0.75), price: 40, slot: "head", tags: ["armor"], armor: 1, strength: 11),
    // The potions, each spent by its use or where it lands when thrown. The
    // good ones do to whoever a thrown one breaks on what they do to their
    // drinker, and a few are wasted thrown; the three that are better
    // thrown burst round their drinker as round wherever they land.
    (name: "potion of healing", glyph: '!', color: (0.95, 0.3, 0.35), price: 40, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     effects: [(kind: "Mend", args: (roll: "3d6+4")), (kind: "Cleanse", args: (status: "poisoned"))],
     triggers: [(on: "use"), (on: "land")]),
    (name: "potion of extra healing", glyph: '!', color: (0.95, 0.4, 0.5), price: 90, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     effects: [(kind: "Mend", args: (roll: "6d6+10")), (kind: "Cleanse", args: (status: "poisoned"))],
     triggers: [(on: "use"), (on: "land")]),
    // Strength and life for good: what heavy gear asks for, and more to
    // lose; and wasted on whatever they are thrown at.
    (name: "potion of strength", glyph: '!', color: (0.85, 0.35, 0.2), price: 300, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Strengthen", args: (by: 1))])]),
    (name: "potion of life", glyph: '!', color: (0.95, 0.85, 0.6), price: 800, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Life", args: (by: 10))])]),
    // Haste, and a skin fire cannot touch, on the drinker or on whoever a
    // thrown one breaks on.
    (name: "potion of haste", glyph: '!', color: (0.6, 0.85, 0.95), price: 60, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     effects: [(kind: "Inflict", args: (status: "hasted", turns: 15))], triggers: [(on: "use"), (on: "land")]),
    (name: "potion of fire immunity", glyph: '!', color: (0.95, 0.6, 0.3), price: 50, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     effects: [(kind: "Inflict", args: (status: "fireproof", turns: 50))], triggers: [(on: "use"), (on: "land")]),
    // Darkness: drunk, the drinker shrouded in a dark of their own; thrown,
    // a cloud of it to hide in where it lands.
    (name: "potion of darkness", glyph: '!', color: (0.3, 0.3, 0.38), price: 30, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Darkness", args: (turns: 40, amount: 150))]),
                (on: "land", area: Burst(radius: 1), effects: [(kind: "Emit", args: (gas: "darkness", amount: 200))])]),
    // Descent: down through the floor, and nowhere from the deepest.
    (name: "potion of descent", glyph: '!', color: (0.55, 0.45, 0.7), price: 50, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Descend")])]),
    // The three better thrown, which burst round their drinker just as
    // round wherever they land: fire, and a cloud that holds whoever
    // breathes it, and one that turns their every step about.
    (name: "potion of incineration", glyph: '!', color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.15), price: 40, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     effects: [(kind: "Harm", args: (kind: "fire", roll: "2d6")), (kind: "Ignite", args: (turns: 3))],
     triggers: [(on: "use", area: Burst(radius: 2), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 255, g: 120, b: 40))),
                (on: "land", area: Burst(radius: 2), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 255, g: 120, b: 40)))]),
    (name: "potion of paralysis", glyph: '!', color: (0.85, 0.5, 0.85), price: 40, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     effects: [(kind: "Emit", args: (gas: "paralytic", amount: 200))],
     triggers: [(on: "use", area: Burst(radius: 1)), (on: "land", area: Burst(radius: 1))]),
    (name: "potion of confusion", glyph: '!', color: (0.5, 0.85, 0.75), price: 30, tags: ["potion"], stack: true, throw: (range: 6),
     consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     effects: [(kind: "Emit", args: (gas: "confusing", amount: 200))],
     triggers: [(on: "use", area: Burst(radius: 1)), (on: "land", area: Burst(radius: 1))]),
    // The scrolls, each spent by its reading. One read onto another thing
    // asks which under the one question every such scroll asks, and of any
    // thing at all; asking still tells it is one of the two that ask, so an
    // unknown one is named as the pack asks, and backing out spends
    // nothing. Two of a kind stack, as potions do, said under their title
    // as written: "2 scrolls titled ZUMOR KA".
    (name: "scroll of enchanting", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 200, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", asks: (prompt: "Read it on which?"), effects: [(kind: "Enchant")])]),
    (name: "scroll of identify", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 40, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", asks: (prompt: "Read it on which?"), effects: [(kind: "Identify")])]),
    (name: "scroll of remove curse", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 40, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "RemoveCurse")])]),
    // The rest are read where the reader stands: away to somewhere far,
    // every staff refilled, the floor mapped, foes in sight set on each
    // other; and two that hurt, a shriek that wakes the floor and monsters
    // called up beside the reader.
    (name: "scroll of teleportation", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 50, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Teleport")])]),
    (name: "scroll of recharging", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 80, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Recharge")])]),
    (name: "scroll of magic mapping", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 60, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "MagicMapping")])]),
    (name: "scroll of discord", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 40, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Discord", args: (turns: 10))])]),
    (name: "scroll of aggravate monsters", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 40, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Aggravate")])]),
    (name: "scroll of summon monsters", glyph: '?', color: (0.92, 0.88, 0.72), price: 60, tags: ["scroll"], stack: true, consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Destroyed),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Summon", args: (fewest: 2, most: 3))])]),
    // ANCHOR: staff
    // The staffs, zapped from the pack: a staff's level is its power and its
    // charges both, found at two and better deeper, and a spent charge comes
    // back over the turns its line says, divided by its level. Each level
    // adds two to a bolt's roll, which keeps a firebolt near the content
    // sheet's (L+1)d4 on average with less to it by luck, five turns of
    // poison, two of slowness, two cells to a blink and a blade to a
    // conjuring. Every bolt is seen to fly.
    (name: "staff of firebolt", glyph: '/', color: (0.85, 0.45, 0.25), price: 250, tags: ["staff"], effect_per_level: (amount: 2),
     consumable: (charges: 0, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept, recharge: 500),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 8)), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 255, g: 120, b: 40)),
                 effects: [(kind: "Harm", args: (kind: "fire", roll: "1d4+1")), (kind: "Ignite", args: (turns: 3))])]),
    // ANCHOR_END: staff
    (name: "staff of lightning", glyph: '/', color: (0.7, 0.75, 1.0), price: 250, tags: ["staff"], effect_per_level: (amount: 2),
     consumable: (charges: 0, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept, recharge: 500),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Beam(range: 8)), look: (glyph: '~', color: (r: 190, g: 210, b: 255)),
                 effects: [(kind: "Harm", args: (kind: "lightning", roll: "1d4+1"))])]),
    (name: "staff of poison", glyph: '/', color: (0.45, 0.8, 0.3), price: 200, tags: ["staff"], effect_per_level: (turns: 5),
     consumable: (charges: 0, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept, recharge: 500),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 8)), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 120, g: 220, b: 80)),
                 effects: [(kind: "Inflict", args: (status: "poisoned", turns: 5))])]),
    (name: "staff of slowness", glyph: '/', color: (0.55, 0.6, 0.75), price: 180, tags: ["staff"], effect_per_level: (turns: 2),
     consumable: (charges: 0, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept, recharge: 500),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 8)), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 150, g: 160, b: 200)),
                 effects: [(kind: "Inflict", args: (status: "slowed", turns: 5))])]),
    (name: "staff of blinking", glyph: '/', color: (0.8, 0.85, 1.0), price: 220, tags: ["staff"], effect_per_level: (amount: 1),
     consumable: (charges: 0, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept, recharge: 1000),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 12), aim: Ground), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 220, g: 230, b: 255)),
                 effects: [(kind: "Blink", args: (reach: 2, per_level: 2))])]),
    (name: "staff of conjuration", glyph: '/', color: (0.75, 0.85, 1.0), price: 220, tags: ["staff"], effect_per_level: (amount: 1),
     consumable: (charges: 0, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept, recharge: 1000),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Conjure", args: (blades: 1, turns: 15))])]),
    // The wands, zapped as a staff is, with a few charges that never come
    // back unless a scroll of recharging puts one back: found with a
    // charge or two, or three to five of the commoner, and enchanting adds
    // one. Every bolt is seen to fly; all but domination may be zapped at a
    // friend as well as a foe.
    (name: "wand of domination", glyph: '~', color: (0.7, 0.5, 0.9), price: 300, tags: ["wand"], found_at: (0, 1),
     consumable: (charges: 1, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 8)), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 200, g: 120, b: 255)), effects: [(kind: "Dominate")])]),
    (name: "wand of teleport other", glyph: '~', color: (0.5, 0.6, 1.0), price: 150, tags: ["wand"], found_at: (0, 2),
     consumable: (charges: 3, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 8), aim: Anyone), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 120, g: 150, b: 255)), effects: [(kind: "TeleportOther")])]),
    (name: "wand of polymorph", glyph: '~', color: (0.9, 0.6, 0.8), price: 150, tags: ["wand"], found_at: (0, 2),
     consumable: (charges: 3, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 8), aim: Anyone), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 255, g: 140, b: 220)), effects: [(kind: "Polymorph")])]),
    (name: "wand of beckoning", glyph: '~', color: (0.9, 0.85, 0.5), price: 120, tags: ["wand"], found_at: (0, 2),
     consumable: (charges: 2, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 8), aim: Anyone), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 255, g: 230, b: 130)), effects: [(kind: "Beckon")])]),
    (name: "wand of plenty", glyph: '~', color: (0.6, 0.85, 0.5), price: 100, tags: ["wand"], found_at: (0, 1),
     consumable: (charges: 1, per_level: 1, when_empty: Kept),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 8), aim: Anyone), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 160, g: 240, b: 120)), effects: [(kind: "Plenty")])]),
    // The rings, worn on either hand, each worth what its level makes it:
    // found at one to three, or cursed below nought and stuck on. A level
    // of regeneration is ten health back a hundred turns, which nothing
    // else gives, and a quarter more from every heal; below nought, none
    // back and a quarter less from every heal a level. A level of wisdom
    // refills every staff carried three tenths faster; of reaping, takes
    // twenty-five turns off each one's next charge for every blow that
    // lands, a swing that sweeps through three foes one blow; of
    // awareness, adds fifteen to the chance a turn of spotting what is
    // hidden.
    (name: "ring of regeneration", glyph: '=', color: (0.9, 0.3, 0.35), price: 300, slot: "left finger", either: true, tags: ["ring"],
     per_level: [("regeneration", 10), ("mending", 25)]),
    (name: "ring of stealth", glyph: '=', color: (0.5, 0.5, 0.6), price: 250, slot: "left finger", either: true, tags: ["ring"], per_level: [("stealth", 10)]),
    (name: "ring of light", glyph: '=', color: (1.0, 0.9, 0.6), price: 250, slot: "left finger", either: true, tags: ["ring"], per_level: [("light", 1)]),
    (name: "ring of wisdom", glyph: '=', color: (0.6, 0.7, 0.95), price: 250, slot: "left finger", either: true, tags: ["ring"], per_level: [("wisdom", 30)]),
    (name: "ring of reaping", glyph: '=', color: (0.75, 0.4, 0.4), price: 300, slot: "left finger", either: true, tags: ["ring"], per_level: [("reaping", 25)]),
    (name: "ring of awareness", glyph: '=', color: (0.85, 0.85, 0.6), price: 250, slot: "left finger", either: true, tags: ["ring"], per_level: [("awareness", 15)]),
    // The lights: the lantern the adventurer walks out of Mereholt with,
    // and a torch, worse to carry and better to throw into a dark room, so
    // found among the thrown things.
    (name: "lantern", glyph: '(', color: (1.0, 0.85, 0.55), price: 40, slot: "light", tags: ["light"], light: (radius: 7, color: (1.0, 0.85, 0.6), flicker: 0.1)),
    (name: "torch", glyph: '(', color: (0.85, 0.55, 0.25), price: 10, slot: "light", tags: ["light", "thrown"], throw: (range: 6), light: (radius: 5, color: (1.0, 0.62, 0.3), flicker: 0.35)),
    // The five artifacts, one to a mini-boss, each carrying its cost in
    // its own row rather than in a level: no tags, so none takes a level,
    // none is found by the ordinary budget, and none wears a face or
    // reads `+?`, which `lore.rs`'s own `Lore::knows` already answers
    // "known" for a kind no family ever drew a face for. Each is coloured
    // as its boss is, in `assets/monsters.ron`, and named in that boss's
    // own `drops`, the one place either is found.
    //
    // The Crown of Grubnak: a flat armor and a wider notice, both the
    // engine's own `armor` and `bestows`; the two more its allies in
    // sight deal is `crown_aura`'s, in `src/artifacts.rs`, the one thing
    // here that reaches somebody other than the wearer.
    (name: "the Crown of Grubnak", glyph: '^', color: (1.0, 0.8, 0.2), price: 1600, tags: ["artifact"], slot: "head", armor: 1, bestows: [("quiet", -2)]),
    // The Widow's Fang: a quick blade, poison and a chance of a web on
    // every hit, and a noise at its wielder's own cell every sixty turns,
    // `Whisper` landed by its own `pulse`.
    (name: "the Widow's Fang", glyph: ')', color: (0.9, 0.2, 0.25), price: 1600, tags: ["artifact"], slot: "main hand", either: true,
     melee: (roll: "1d4+2", kind: "pierce", unaware: 500),
     triggers: [(on: "hit", effects: [(kind: "Inflict", args: (status: "poisoned", turns: 4)), (kind: "Inflict", chance: 25, args: (status: "webbed", turns: 1))]),
                (on: "pulse", every: 6000, effects: [(kind: "Whisper")])]),
    // The Choirmaster's Staff: a two-hander with no blow of its own,
    // `RaiseAlly` aimed at a body within six, two charges and a mending
    // of minus ten while it is held.
    (name: "the Choirmaster's Staff", glyph: '_', color: (0.85, 0.85, 1.0), price: 1600, tags: ["artifact"], slot: "main hand", also: ["off hand"],
     bestows: [("mending", -10)], consumable: (charges: 2, when_empty: Kept, recharge: 300),
     triggers: [(on: "use", targeting: (mode: Bolt(range: 6), aim: Ground), look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 220, g: 220, b: 255)),
                 effects: [(kind: "RaiseAlly", args: (turns: 30))])]),
    // The Abbess's Chalice: carried rather than worn, one charge of Mend
    // 15 that `src/artifacts.rs`'s own `refill_chalice` tops up on every
    // new floor rather than on `consumable`'s own clock, and `AlertDrowned`
    // on every drink.
    (name: "the Abbess's Chalice", glyph: '!', color: (0.4, 0.75, 0.7), price: 1600, tags: ["artifact"], consumable: (charges: 1, when_empty: Kept),
     triggers: [(on: "use", effects: [(kind: "Mend", args: (roll: "15")), (kind: "AlertDrowned")])]),
    // The Forgemaster's Hammer: a two-handed sweep that ignites what it
    // strikes, strength nineteen, two hundred a blow, and the loudest
    // step there is, louder than plate's own plus three.
    (name: "the Forgemaster's Hammer", glyph: ')', color: (1.0, 0.5, 0.15), price: 1600, tags: ["artifact"], slot: "main hand", also: ["off hand"], strength: 19, cost: 200,
     bestows: [("footfall", 6)],
     melee: (roll: "3d6+3", kind: "crush", shape: Sweep, look: (glyph: '*', color: (r: 255, g: 120, b: 40))),
     triggers: [(on: "hit", effects: [(kind: "Ignite", args: (turns: 3))])]),
    // A pile is three to twenty-four coins on floor one, and floor times
    // that further down; a floor's piles are laid besides its things, and
    // what the dead leave is their own.
    (name: "gold coin", glyph: '$', color: (1.0, 0.85, 0.3), tags: ["gold"], stack: true, pile: "3d8"),
]
